    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Property Partners Gill & Glynn are pleased to bring to market this impressive 4 bedroom, contemporary family home, located just 3 kms outside the idyllic village of Cong. Surrounded by lush countryside, Drumsheel is set in one of the most stunning locations in the west of Ireland.\n\nACCOMADATION\n\nAccommodation extends to 234.41 sq. m. (2,524 sq. ft) and sits on approximately 1.2 acres of private grounds, with an additional 6 acres to the rear of the house currently included with the property, together with the option to acquire a further 5 acres located directly across from the house, providing up to approximately 11 additional acres in total, available either as a whole or in separate lots, subject to agreement.\n\nThe property is accessed through electric gates and opens onto a welcoming entrance hall, with a sweeping staircase and balcony-style upstairs landing. The spacious living room is located to the rear of the property, featuring an electric fireplace with a sleek white mantelpiece. A set of large sliding doors opens onto the gravel driveway at the rear of the property. The living room flows seamlessly into the combined kitchen and dining area. This light-filled space includes white shaker-style cabinetry and a window seat nestled neatly between the kitchen units. There is a built-in double oven and microwave, together with an integrated fridge.\n\nLocated just off the kitchen is a large utility room with ample storage, an elevated washing machine and tumble dryer, providing excellent practicality for everyday family life. A second laundry room is located upstairs, also equipped with a washing machine and tumble dryer. A thoughtfully designed laundry chute links the upstairs laundry room directly to the downstairs laundry room, making household chores particularly convenient for busy family living. \n\n To the left of the entrance hall is a cosy sitting room. The property also benefits from a generous ground floor bedroom with built-in wardrobes and a Jack and Jill ensuite bathroom, providing access from both the bedroom and the main hall for guests.\n\nThe first floor comprises of three spacious bedrooms, all with built-in wardrobes. The master bedroom features a generous walk-in wardrobe and a stylish ensuite bathroom. The bathrooms throughout the home are finished with contemporary floor-to-ceiling tiling, sleek chrome fittings and wet room style showers. The family bathroom is further enhanced by a stylish claw-foot bath.\n\nThere is a large walk-in hot press together with additional attic storage, accessed via a Stira staircase from one of the bedrooms.\n\nCombining comfort with efficiency, the home benefits from geothermal under floor heating throughout, with insulation incorporated within the floors, as well as a new heat recovery ventilation system designed toi improve air quality and energy efficiency. The property also benefits from triple-glazed windows and a composite front door, further enhancing the homes thermal performance, comfort and security. Fibre broadband, providing fast and reliable connectivity for work, entertainment and everyday living.\n\nExternally, the property features an impressive stone-clad façade, a gravel driveway that wraps around the house, and a paved patio area. The home is approached through electric entrance gates, enhancing both privacy and security. A detached garage is located to the rear of the property and benefits from substantial 6-inch cavity wall construction, providing excellent insulation and storage potential.\n\nLOCATION\n\nCong is a village straddling the borders of County Galway and County Mayo. Cong is located on the isthmus connecting Loughs Corrib and Mask, near the towns of Headford and Ballinrobe and the villages of Neale and Cross. It is well known and renowned for many tourist attractions such as Ashford Castle, location of the Quiet Man film, lake cruises and historic sights. The land is just minutes from the popular Ashford Castle and all that Cong has to offer while it is also commuting distance to the bustling city of Galway.\nVIEWING\nThis property is likely to appeal to a wide variety of purchasers and truly must be viewed to be fully appreciated.\n\nAn early inspection is highly recommended. In addition to business hours, viewings can usually be accommodated in the evenings and at weekends.\n\nTo arrange a viewing, call or text our negotiator handling this sale, Emma Gill, on 087 799 9955 or 091 884000.\n\n\nAttention is drawn to this important notice. \nProperty Partners Gill & Glynn for themselves and for the vendors or lessors of this property whose agents they are, give notice that:\n(i) The particulars are set out as a general outline for the guidance of intending purchasers or lessees, and do not constitute, nor constitute part of, an offer or contract.\n(ii) All descriptions, dimensions, references to condition and necessary permissions for use and occupation, and other details are given in good faith and are believed to be correct, but any intending purchasers or tenants should not rely on them as statements or representations of fact but must satisfy themselves by inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of each of them. \n(iii) We have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. \n(iv) All measurements are approximate and photographs and maps provided are for guidance only.\n"
      },
